@startuml
title Student Feature — Sequence Diagram (Specify)
autonumber

actor Student
participant "Student Experience" as UI
participant "Student Feature" as SF
participant "Shared Foundation" as Foundation
participant "Shared Session Data" as Data
actor Teacher

Student -> UI : enter Activity Code
UI -> SF : request activity lookup
SF -> Foundation : restricted anonymous lookup
Foundation -> Data : resolve code and phase
Data --> Foundation : activity summary
Foundation --> SF : limited summary
SF --> UI : show activity and join choices

Student -> UI : choose Team and join
UI -> SF : join request
SF -> SF : establish verified activity-scoped Participant identity\n[passwordless; recoverable in same browser]
SF -> Data : create or confirm membership
Data --> SF : membership relation
SF --> UI : joined activity
note over SF,Data
The server atomically assigns the first successful member as leader.
Transient disconnect preserves that role; pre-start team change needs
explicit handoff. Permanent loss requires authorized Teacher transfer.
end note

UI -> Foundation : watch Session
Foundation -> Foundation : authorize verified ActorContext
Foundation --> UI : latest SessionStateSnapshot
Foundation --> UI : session:state:changed on later updates

alt Waiting or no current Round
  UI -> UI : show waiting; do not request target content
else Active
  UI -> Foundation : request current target
  Foundation -> Foundation : enforce Participant, Team and Active phase
  Foundation -> Data : read Question / QuestionGroup / Blanks
  Data --> Foundation : structured target
  Foundation --> UI : current target
  Student -> UI : edit one or more answers
  UI -> SF : update shared Team/Round draft
  SF -> SF : persist accepted Blank value\n[Student-owned persistence]
  SF --> UI : share updated draft with team members
  note over UI,SF
  Same-Blank conflicts use the last server-accepted edit.
  Reload/reconnect restores the saved draft. This is Student-owned;
  Foundation state events do not carry answer drafts.
  end note
  opt authorized team leader submits
    Student -> UI : submit answers
    UI -> SF : submit current Round and Blank values
    SF -> SF : verify actor, leader, phase, values and no prior Team/Round submission
    SF -> Data : persist one Submission and SubmissionAnswers\nwith server-assigned acceptedOrder
    Data --> SF : accepted Submission or validation/conflict error
    SF --> UI : submission outcome
    alt Submission accepted
      SF -> SF : freeze shared draft as read-only
      SF --> UI : notify team members that draft is locked
    else Submission rejected
      SF --> UI : keep draft editable; show safe error
    end
  end
end

Teacher -> SF : request winner for Round during End
SF -> Data : select earliest accepted Submission by acceptedOrder
Data --> SF : winning Submission or no winner
SF --> Teacher : trusted winner candidate
Teacher -> Foundation : end Round with supplied winner (or none)
Foundation -> Data : commit Ended state and supplied Result atomically
Data --> Foundation : committed state / Result
Foundation --> UI : session:state:changed (Ended)
UI -> SF : request student result view after Ended
SF -> Data : read persisted Result, winning Team and answer rows
Data --> SF : authorized winning Team and accepted answers
SF --> UI : winning Team and answers only

note over SF,Data
No client-supplied Team, role or acceptedOrder is trusted.
Repeated watch/reconnect reconciles to the latest snapshot.
No draft-edit Socket.IO event is defined by Foundation.
end note
@enduml
